    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for unbound.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The unbound packages provide a validating, recursive, and caching DNS or DNSSEC resolver. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* unbound: Unbound: Denial of Service via excessive EDNS options (CVE-2026-41292)\n\n* unbound: Unbound: Cache manipulation via 'ghost domain names' attack (CVE-2026-40622)\n\n* unbound: Unbound: Denial of Service due to excessive resource consumption with large DNS Resource Record Sets (CVE-2026-44390)\n\n* unbound: Unbound: Denial of Service due to degraded resolution performance in jostle logic (CVE-2026-42534)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
        "title": "Terms of Use"
      }
